,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Good repository practices","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"rTh8UJJMt9"}],"identifier":"good-repository-practices","label":"Good repository practices","html_id":"good-repository-practices","implicit":true,"key":"BSBQC6dZpa"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work as a team. Work collaboratively with your team members by adding commit messages and working in different branches, merging them into the main branch as your group sees fit. Also, consider taking advantage of issues as you review each other’s work asynchronously, and even consider opening issues and opening PRs that close them, as we practiced in Peer Review 2.","position":{"start":{"line":55,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"key":"bws7VGz6F8"}],"key":"PP7KmdrUYE"}],"key":"GPmiZM17tk"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"README.md","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"IGddV9plUj"},{"type":"text","value":": Write a short self-contained description of the project, including the motivation behind your project and the analysis you conducted. Include all relevant information about how to run the analysis, including installation steps (for any packages, environments, etc.), testing, and automation. A good README should be short but also provide all the useful information to help the user to start running the analysis.","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"LzhBfXDStp"}],"key":"VKM8ksN2dh"}],"key":"MeLzcNrYrT"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LICENSE","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"W283S7u5jy"},{"type":"text","value":": you should explicitly state which licensing conditions apply to your work (see ","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"rZx0R0MBjo"},{"type":"link","url":"https://help.github.com/articles/adding-a-license-to-a-repository/","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Github’s help","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"DfzKp8Wwwj"}],"urlSource":"https://help.github.com/articles/adding-a-license-to-a-repository/","key":"hOkQ4EZqR4"},{"type":"text","value":"). We strongly suggest looking at Victoria Stodden’s ","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"lrVrHeSGQZ"},{"type":"link","url":"https://stodden.net/papers/ijclp-STODDEN-2009.pdf","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ENABLING REPRODUCIBLE RESEARCH:\nLICENSING SCIENTIFIC INNOVATION","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"L1dSGqdG6X"}],"urlSource":"https://stodden.net/papers/ijclp-STODDEN-2009.pdf","key":"osvnZMLPxu"},{"type":"text","value":". She suggests a “Reproducible research standard” that licenses code, data and text/media materials in comparable terms that maximize resharing potential while providing due credit guarantees for the original authors.","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"UXJLwxa7Ty"}],"key":"yOnaqS0thI"}],"key":"Cwftq1JywA"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".gitignore","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"FiIxAbJltn"},{"type":"text","value":": provide a git ignore file that prevents the automatic inclusion of unwanted files. This also helps you avoid noisy ","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"ppngkf9jVe"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git status","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"eIMEya7131"},{"type":"text","value":" output that lists things you know you won’t actually want to put under git’s control.","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"H1TtWlE1Zk"}],"key":"kA9njMDXx8"}],"key":"qRmMpFopNj"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A ","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"EdhX58Otpu"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"binder","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"mXkkwEkFaN"},{"type":"text","value":" link: also deploy your repository on Binder, including the badge in your repository and ensuring that all notebooks can be executed for enhanced reproducibility.","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"zTELrae3YY"}],"key":"AUI7ZK9lIi"}],"key":"XxZevE8yU0"}],"key":"fGmR4JvsCJ"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Website","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"peT0Jf9Jji"}],"identifier":"website","label":"Website","html_id":"website","implicit":true,"key":"TYGVMbrbHz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finally, we ask that you deploy your analyses to a MyST-generated website, hosted on GitHub Pages. Please take the time to consider how to best organize your websites to communicate the overall narrative of your project, from the main narrative document, to the individual analysis notebooks. Please also include the Binder badge somewhere in the website.","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"LB4ng5cDdx"}],"key":"PMYbwVt72M"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Release","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"oRsheZ6G1Z"}],"identifier":"release","label":"Release","html_id":"release","implicit":true,"key":"OVGaXzpVbm"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We also ask that you tag your repository on GitHub when you are finished, marking a version release of your project. We also ask that each of you make an ORCID, archive your release on Zenodo and reference the ORCIDs of your group members, and then include the resulting DOI with a DOI badge in your GitHub repository. See the Lecture 12 slides on how to do this.","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"jO9QlJVn3B"}],"key":"WwDRuezgqh"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grading","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"jQwlIRwVWr"}],"identifier":"grad